    <section id="cc_capabilities" class="cc_capabilities" aria-labelledby="cc_capabilities_title">
        <div class="cc_section_heading">
            <span class="cc_section_kicker">More than a chart maker</span>
            <h2 id="cc_capabilities_title">From raw rows to a defensible answer.</h2>
            <p>Crossex keeps the entire exploratory workflow together, so the path from source data to final view stays visible and repeatable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cc_capability_grid">
            <article class="cc_capability_card cc_capability_featured">
                <div class="cc_capability_icon" aria-hidden="true">⌁</div>
                <div>
                    <span class="cc_capability_label">Explore visually</span>
                    <h3>Map columns. The right view appears.</h3>
                    <p>Choose X, Y, color, size, opacity, or facets. Crossex reads the data types and moves naturally between scatter, line, histogram, ECDF, QQ, box, violin, heatmap, correlation, overview, and 3D views.</p>
                    <div class="cc_feature_tags"><span>Faceting</span><span>Regression</span><span>Contours</span><span>40+ palettes</span><span>PNG · SVG · CSV</span></div>
                </div>
            </article>
            <article class="cc_capability_card">
                <div class="cc_capability_icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</div>
                <span class="cc_capability_label">Understand the data</span>
                <h3>See quality issues before they become chart issues.</h3>
                <p>Inspect inferred types, missing values, distinct counts, examples, and warnings. Override types safely, then use summaries, statistical annotations, normality checks, and correlations.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="cc_capability_card">
                <div class="cc_capability_icon" aria-hidden="true">ƒx</div>
                <span class="cc_capability_label">Prepare and reshape</span>
                <h3>Do the useful table work without leaving the browser.</h3>
                <p>Create formula columns, filter, sort, deduplicate, group, append, and join. Every operation creates a new immutable state that you can undo or redo.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="cc_capability_card cc_capability_wide">
                <div class="cc_capability_icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</div>
                <div>
                    <span class="cc_capability_label">Reproduce and communicate</span>
                    <h3>Keep the analysis, not just the screenshot.</h3>
                    <p>Export a portable project with data, settings, formulas, and provenance; restore it later; share a compressed view; arrange dashboards; or embed the same explorer in a web page, RStudio, Shiny, or R Markdown.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="cc_repro_stack" aria-hidden="true"><span>03 · grouped by species</span><span>02 · added BMI formula</span><span>01 · loaded penguins.csv</span></div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="cc_workflow" aria-label="Three-step workflow">
        <div><span>01</span><b>Bring a table</b><p>Paste it, open a file, or load a URL.</p></div>
        <div><span>02</span><b>Follow the question</b><p>Map columns, inspect patterns, and refine.</p></div>
        <div><span>03</span><b>Keep the trail</b><p>Export the view, project, data, or dashboard.</p></div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="cc_start_section" class="cc_start" aria-labelledby="cc_start_title">
<div id="cc_start_intro" class="cc_start_intro">
    <span class="cc_section_kicker">Try it now</span>
    <h2 id="cc_start_title">Start with your data—or ours.</h2>
    <p>Paste a table below, drop in a file, fetch a public URL, or open the demo. Your data is processed locally in this tab.</p>
</div>
<form id="cc_data_form">
    <label class="cc_sr_only" for="myccinput">Paste CSV, TSV, or JSON data</label>
    <textarea id="myccinput" placeholder="Paste CSV, TSV, or JSON data here — or drag and drop a file" style="width:100%;height:90px;font-size:xx-small;"></textarea>
    <input type="file" id="ccfileinput" accept=".csv,.tsv,.txt,.tab,.json" style="display:none">
    <div class="cc_input_actions">
        <button type="button" id="graph_button" class="cc_button active">Graph Data</button>
        <button type="button" id="load_file" class="cc_button">Load File</button>
        <button type="button" id="load_url" class="cc_button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cc_url_bar">Load URL</button>
        <button type="button" id="build_dashboard" class="cc_button">Dashboard</button>
        <button type="button" id="default_data" class="cc_button">Load Demo Data</button>
        <button type="button" id="large_demo" class="cc_button">Load 5M Demo</button>
        <button type="button" id="data_quality" class="cc_button" disabled>Data Quality</button>
        <button type="button" id="share_link" class="cc_button">Share Link</button>
        <button type="button" id="dark_toggle" class="cc_button" aria-pressed="false">Dark Mode</button>
        <button type="button" id="clear_cookies" class="cc_button">Clear Settings</button>
    </div>
    <div id="cc_url_bar" class="cc_url_bar" role="region" aria-label="Load data from URL" style="display:none">
        <label class="cc_sr_only" for="cc_url_field">CSV, TSV, or JSON URL</label>
        <input type="url" id="cc_url_field" class="cc_url_field" inputmode="url" autocomplete="url"
            placeholder="https://example.com/data.csv — a CSV, TSV, or JSON table">
        <button type="button" id="cc_url_go" class="cc_button active">Fetch &amp; Graph</button>
        <button type="button" id="cc_url_cancel" class="cc_button">Cancel</button>
    </div>
</form>
</section>
<div id="cc_data_notice" class="cc_data_notice" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>
    <span id="cc_data_notice_text"></span>
    <button type="button" id="cc_data_notice_close" aria-label="Dismiss message">&times;</button>
</div>
<section id="cc_quality" class="cc_quality" aria-labelledby="cc_quality_title" hidden>
    <div class="cc_quality_head">
        <div>
            <h3 id="cc_quality_title" tabindex="-1">Data quality and column types</h3>
            <p id="cc_quality_summary"></p>
        </div>
        <button type="button" id="cc_quality_close" class="cc_quality_close" aria-label="Close data quality panel">&times;</button>
    </div>
    <div id="cc_quality_issues" class="cc_quality_issues"></div>
    <div class="cc_quality_table_wrap">
        <table class="cc_quality_table">
            <thead><tr><th>Column</th><th>Detected</th><th>Missing</th><th>Distinct</th><th>Example values</th><th>Use as</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody id="cc_quality_columns"></tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <div class="cc_quality_actions">
        <button type="button" id="cc_quality_apply" class="cc_button active">Apply type changes and regraph</button>
        <span>Invalid numeric or date values become missing.</span>
    </div>
</section>
